# Viability against fecundity selection

2000 generations after the move; strata weighted equally; 95% stratified bootstrap intervals (2000 resamples of inputs within strata).

## NoQTL ≤ 1000

Fixed size: 900 inputs (NoQTL 100, u 3: 150; NoQTL 100, u 5: 150; NoQTL 500, u 3: 150; NoQTL 500, u 5: 150; NoQTL 1000, u 3: 150; NoQTL 1000, u 5: 150).

### Fixed size (QTSim's demography)

| | viability | fecundity |
|:--|--:|--:|
| died before the move | 0 | 0 |
| alive 2000 generations after the move | 7.2% (5.7–8.9) | 49.1% (45.7–52.3) |
| median generations to extinction (those that died) | 124 (115–133) | 975 (875–1045) |
| died after the move (of 900) | 835 | 458 |
| median generations to 50% mortality (W̄ ≈ 0.5 for fecundity) | 45 (41–48) | 45 (42–49) |
| median standardised lag | 0.349 (0.322–0.387) | 0.299 (0.268–0.339) |
| N·W̄ never below 2 within 2000 generations | – | 14.0% (11.8–16.2) |
| median generations until N·W̄ < 2 (those that got there) | – | 128 (120–136) |

Paired by input:

- time to extinction, fecundity / viability (median over 458 inputs where both died after the move): 12.00 (11.86–12.15)
- generations until N·W̄ < 2 under fecundity / time to extinction under viability (median over 774 inputs): 1.11 (1.09–1.12)
- alive under viability but dead under fecundity: 0; the reverse: 377 (McNemar exact p = 6.5e-114)

